{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>With what.</b> If each one of you says: With what shall I appease my Elohim, who did this kindness with my fathers? And this is the sense of <b>with what shall I come</b> [Micah 6:6]. And the word אכף [from the root כפף, to bow] is of the doubled-conjugation [binyan pi'el/pu'al type], like אשתחוה, in the manner of one who brings a gift to his lord."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:05.826704822Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}